        "original_id": "c794d138-5a8a-5370-9174-c981af212b50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Pirner, Les McKeown, Harvey Shield, Butch Vig\n- Bands: Soul Asylum, Bay City Rollers\n- Songs: \"Just Like Anyone\", \"The Way I Feel Tonight\"\n- Roles: lead vocalist, frontman, lead singer, songwriter, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Dave Pirner, born April 16, 1964, is an American songwriter, singer, and producer best known as the lead vocalist and frontman of Soul Asylum.\n- Les McKeown, born 12 November 1955, is a Scottish pop singer who was the lead singer of the Bay City Rollers during their most successful period.\n- \"Just Like Anyone\" was written by Dave Pirner and produced by Soul Asylum with Butch Vig, and it was released as the album's second single.\n- \"The Way I Feel Tonight\" was written by Harvey Shield and features a lead vocal by Les McKeown.\n- \"The Way I Feel Tonight\" is a slow, dramatic ballad with a heavily orchestrated arrangement.",
